class Solution {
    public int hammingWeight(int n) {
        int count = 0;

        while (n != 0) {
            if ((n & 1) == 1) {
                count++;
            }
            n = n >>> 1;
        }

        return count;
    }
}

**Time:** `O(32)` → `O(1)`
**Space:** `O(1)`

### Why `>>>`?

* `>>` = signed right shift → keeps the sign bit (`1` for negative numbers).
* `>>>` = unsigned right shift → fills left bits with `0`.

We use `>>>` because `n` is a **32-bit integer** and can be negative. With `>>>`, the bits are shifted out and `n` eventually becomes `0`.
